= Consensus mechanism — Technical =

Consensus protocols are analyzed through properties such as agreement/safety and termination/liveness under an explicit failure model. Blockchain designs add leader/proposer selection, Sybil resistance, fork choice, economic incentives, and finality mechanisms to classical distributed-consensus concerns.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* consensus mechanism ≠ majority vote
* consensus ≠ unanimity
* consensus ≠ unconditional finality

== References ==
* NIST IR 8202, ''Blockchain Technology Overview'' (2018).
* NIST CSRC glossary, “Consensus model”: process to achieve agreement within a distributed system on the valid state.
* Miguel Castro & Barbara Liskov, “Practical Byzantine Fault Tolerance” (1999), for Byzantine consensus foundations.
